# This context is shared by two Dockerfiles:
#   - .devcontainer/Dockerfile (devcontainer.json sets context to "..",
#     i.e. the project root) — does not COPY or ADD anything.
#   - the root Dockerfile (release image) — `COPY . .` for
#     `cargo build --features bundled -p thunderduck-connect-server`.
#
# Without this file the context would include multi-GB directories
# (target/, .claude/worktrees/, test parquet data), which Podman streams
# into /var/tmp on the VM and runs out of space.
#
# Default-deny, then allowlist exactly what the release Dockerfile's cargo
# build needs. If you add a COPY/ADD elsewhere, whitelist the new path here.

*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!crates/
!crates/**
!extensions/vendored/
!extensions/vendored/**
